   "**March:** inflows 50,000; outflows 40,000; opening (5,000) &rarr; net +10,000 &rarr; **closing 5,000**",
   "Note the three rules: a positive net cash flow **increases** the closing balance; a negative one **reduces** it; and each closing balance **becomes** the next opening balance. Get these three right and you can complete any forecast in the exam."
